      "body": "a simple reproducer\n\nand this exists also in 3.13 and 3.14\n\n```py\n# cpython git:(main) ✗ ./python.exe tt.py \n# [1]    49904 segmentation fault  ./python.exe tt.py\n# cpython git:(main) ✗ cat tt.py \nco = compile(\"def f(): pass\", '<string>', 'exec')\nco = co.replace(co_consts=(b'A',))\nexec(co)\n```\n\n--- \nseems need to check the type in `PyFunction_NewWithQualName`\nbut it maybe lower the performance I wonder",
