      "body": "I'm not really sure we should consider messing with `co_*` fields as legitimate. We do have some checks here and there, but I think we shouldn't do much. It's known that putting garbage in `co_consts` will lead to errors as it'd no more relevant to the rest of the code object.\n\nThere is an open issue about it: https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/122850 which planned to disallow arbitrary objects but it wouldn't help in this case I think.\n\ncc @encukou ",
