      "created_at": "2025-10-31T13:50:07Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-10-31T13:50:07Z",
      "body": "This has nothing to do with the `textwrap` module. You messed with the bytecode object, you break some invariants, you get an undefined behavior. The bug is not in Python, but in the user code.\n\nThere are many other ways to trigger a crash by messing with the code object.  Correctness of the bytecode cannot be checked in principle, and correctness of other code object attributes is not checked (apart from a superficial check) for performance reasons.",
